// Route-group index (routes/(marketing)/index.treaty).
//
// A directory wrapped in parentheses is a ROUTE GROUP: it organises files
// without (conceptually) contributing a URL segment, letting marketing pages
// share a folder. The scanner records the group; downstream tooling flattens
// it. This is the group's own index route.

<section class="marketing-home">
  <h1>Marketing</h1>
  <p>Grouped marketing pages live here.</p>
</section>
